"""Introductory PDTB 3.0-inspired teaching questions; simplified for classroom use."""
QUESTIONS = [
('The roads were flooded because it rained heavily.','Which word explicitly signals the discourse relation?',['roads','because','flooded','heavily'],1,'Because is the explicit connective introducing a causal explanation.'),
('Although the article was long, the students read it.','Which broad PDTB relation class best describes the contrast?',['Temporal','Expansion','Comparison','Contingency'],2,'Although introduces a concessive contrast, grouped under Comparison.'),
('The experiment failed because the equipment broke.','What is the broad relation class?',['Contingency','Temporal','Expansion','Comparison'],0,'Because signals a causal relation, part of Contingency.'),
('The students revised the chapter. Then they completed the quiz.','What is the broad relation class?',['Comparison','Temporal','Contingency','Expansion'],1,'Then orders events in time, indicating a Temporal relation.'),
('The paper discusses syntax. It also examines semantics.','Which broad relation class fits the additive link?',['Expansion','Comparison','Temporal','Contingency'],0,'Also adds related information, a form of Expansion.'),
('Sara stayed home because she was ill.','Which span is Arg2 for the connective because?',['Sara stayed home','she was ill','Sara','stayed home'],1,'For an explicit subordinating connective such as because, Arg2 is the clause syntactically linked to the connective.'),
('Sara stayed home because she was ill.','Which span is Arg1?',['she was ill','because','Sara stayed home','ill'],2,'Arg1 is the other argument: Sara stayed home.'),
('The weather was cold. However, they went hiking.','What is the explicit connective?',['weather','cold','However','hiking'],2,'However explicitly marks a contrast between the propositions.'),
('The weather was cold. However, they went hiking.','Which broad relation class is most suitable?',['Comparison','Temporal','Expansion','Contingency'],0,'However introduces contrast, a Comparison relation.'),
('He missed the bus. He arrived late.','If the causal relation is inferred without an overt connective, what annotation type is appropriate?',['Explicit','Implicit','EntRel','NoRel'],1,'An inferred relation without an overt connective can be annotated as Implicit; an appropriate inserted connective could be because/as a result.'),
('The teacher explained the rule, and the students took notes.','Which word is the explicit connective?',['teacher','explained','and','notes'],2,'And connects the two discourse arguments.'),
('The teacher explained the rule, and the students took notes.','Which broad class best fits the additive interpretation?',['Expansion','Comparison','Temporal','Contingency'],0,'On the intended additive reading, and expresses Expansion. Context can permit other readings.'),
('Before the lecture began, students opened their notebooks.','What broad class does before signal?',['Expansion','Temporal','Comparison','Contingency'],1,'Before locates one event in time relative to another.'),
('If the data are incomplete, the analysis may be misleading.','What broad class does if signal?',['Comparison','Expansion','Contingency','Temporal'],2,'If introduces a condition, part of Contingency.'),
('The result was surprising. In addition, it was statistically significant.','What is the connective?',['result','surprising','In addition','significant'],2,'In addition explicitly signals additive information.'),
('The result was surprising. In addition, it was statistically significant.','Which broad relation class applies?',['Expansion','Temporal','Comparison','Contingency'],0,'Adding another property is an Expansion relation.'),
('While Sara prepared the slides, Ali checked the projector.','Which broad relation class fits the simultaneous-events reading?',['Temporal','Comparison','Contingency','Expansion'],0,'While can signal temporal overlap; in this sentence the intended reading is simultaneous events.'),
('Even though the dataset was small, the model performed well.','Which broad class fits the concessive reading?',['Contingency','Comparison','Expansion','Temporal'],1,'Even though signals concession, which belongs to Comparison in this introductory classification.'),
('The students submitted the assignment. The instructor graded it.','What is the most defensible annotation principle?',['Always choose Temporal','Always choose Expansion','Use context and guidelines to determine the relation','Never annotate adjacent sentences'],2,'Adjacent sentences may support different relations; annotators should rely on context and the PDTB guidelines.'),
('In PDTB annotation, what do Arg1 and Arg2 denote?','Choose the best answer.',['Two discourse arguments linked by a relation','The subject and object of one verb','Two POS tags','Two annotators'],0,'Arg1 and Arg2 are discourse argument spans, not necessarily grammatical subjects or objects.'),
]
